retries were exhausted. The deciding
agent can then tolerate specialist failures without also tolerating a failed
mode/scope preflight: synthesize separately requires both to have succeeded.', NULL, '$scope.output.head_matches == true', ARRAY['scope', 'route', 'seams', 'code', 'tests', 'errors', 'docs']::text[], 'all_done', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'true', NULL, 'archon-review-block', 'review/archon-review-block.yaml');
INSERT INTO mc.arch_steps (archon_sha, factory_sha, workflow, path, parent_path, position, step_id, kind, description, model, when_condition, depends_on, trigger_rule, include, child_workflow, round_cap, command, command_file, script, script_file, runtime, bash, prompt, defined_in, file) VALUES ('57c8574020000000000000000000000000000000', '6311108f789119a8a1a6a7c77ece21ca3a75c3e8', 'archon-ship-block', 'deliver/rounds/review/synthesize', 'deliver/rounds/review', 34, 'synthesize', 'command', 'A failed specialist (a provider stream dying mid-review, say) must not kill
the review: synthesize detects the missing completion for a selected lens and
forces ready:false naming the gap, so degradation is disclosed, never silent,
and the next round is the retry. `ready` is a real boolean — the load-bearing field a composing
loop terminates on. Every round receives this round''s lens files; a
continuation also receives the complete prior report and correction delta.

The deciding agent and the lenses start fresh and carry earlier rounds through
the prior report, not a resumed session: a loop body cannot resume a session
from its own earlier iteration, and session resume is not portable across the
bundle''s supported providers (Claude Code, Codex, and Pi).

Adversarial per-finding verification happens inside this node''s prompt. A
separate verify stage between the lenses and this node is now expressible and
would not change either side''s contract — the findings files are the declared
boundary — but nothing has measured it as better than the in-prompt pass, so
it stays here until something does.', '@reviewer medium', '$scope.output.head_matches == true', ARRAY['policy', 'mode', 'scope', 'review-complete']::text[], NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'review-synthesize', 'review/commands/review-synthesize.md', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'archon-review-block', 'review/archon-review-block.yaml');
INSERT INTO mc.arch_steps (archon_sha, factory_sha, workflow, path, parent_path, position, step_id, kind, description, model, when_condition, depends_on, trigger_rule, include, child_workflow, round_cap, command, command_file, script, script_file, runtime, bash, prompt, defined_in, file) VALUES ('57c8574020000000000000000000000000000000', '6311108f789119a8a1a6a7c77ece21ca3a75c3e8', 'archon-ship-block', 'deliver/rounds/review/publish', 'deliver/rounds/review', 35, 'publish', 'script', 'The reviewer judges and writes the report; this node owns the one public
write, so every round edits the same marked comment instead of appending
another, through whichever forge source the run selected (on `gh`, a landed
write that returned a retryable response (5xx, or a rate limit) or no response can leave a second one, and the next
upsert refuses). The verdict passes
through unchanged: publication is not what makes a review true.', NULL, '$scope.output.head_matches == true', ARRAY['synthesize']::text[], NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'publish-review', 'review/scripts/publish-review.ts', 'bun', NULL, NULL, 'archon-review-block', 'review/archon-review-block.yaml');
INSERT INTO mc.arch_steps (archon_sha, factory_sha, workflow, path, parent_path, position, step_id, kind, description, model, when_condition, depends_on, trigger_rule, include, child_workflow, round_cap, command, command_file, script, script_file, runtime, bash, prompt, defined_in, file) VALUES ('57c8574020000000000000000000000000000000', '6311108f789119a8a1a6a7c77ece21ca3a75c3e8', 'archon-ship-block', 'deliver/rounds/review/result', 'deliver/rounds/review', 36, 'result', 'script', 'Standalone runs show the first completed sink, so the verdict precedes cleanup.', NULL, NULL, ARRAY['scope', 'publish']::text[], 'none_failed_min_one_success', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'const verdict = JSON.parse(process.env.INPUTS_VERDICT);
const report = JSON.parse(process.env.INPUTS_SCOPE_REPORT);
console.log(JSON.stringify(JSON.parse(process.env.INPUTS_HEAD_MATCHES) ? verdict : {
  ready: false, action: "ask",
  findings_summary: require("node:fs").readFileSync(require("node:path").join(process.env.ARTIFACTS_DIR, report.path), "utf8"),
  report, discoveries: [], contract_left: ["PR head mismatch prevented contract review."]
}));
', NULL, 'bun', NULL, NULL, 'archon-review-block', 'review/archon-review-block.yaml');
INSERT INTO mc.arch_steps (archon_sha, factory_sha, workflow, path, parent_path, position, step_id, kind, description, model, when_condition, depends_on, trigger_rule, include, child_workflow, round_cap, command, command_file, script, script_file, runtime, bash, prompt, defined_in, file) VALUES ('57c8574020000000000000000000000000000000', '6311108f789119a8a1a6a7c77ece21ca3a75c3e8', 'archon-ship-block', 'deliver/rounds/review/prune-scratch', 'deliver/rounds/review', 37, 'prune-scratch', 'script', 'Reviewers'' scratch worktrees are removed by the workflow once every lens and
the deciding agent have settled, whether they succeeded or failed.', NULL, NULL, ARRAY['synthesize']::text[], 'all_done', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'prune-scratch', 'review/scripts/prune-scratch.ts', 'bun', NULL, NULL, 'archon-review-block', 'review/archon-review-block.yaml');
INSERT INTO mc.arch_steps (archon_sha, factory_sha, workflow, path, parent_path, position, step_id, kind, description, model, when_condition, depends_on, trigger_rule, include, child_workflow, round_cap, command, command_file, script, script_file, runtime, bash, prompt, defined_in, file) VALUES ('57c8574020000000000000000000000000000000', '6311108f789119a8a1a6a7c77ece21ca3a75c3e8', 'archon-ship-block', 'deliver/rounds/simplify', 'deliver/rounds', 38, 'simplify', 'include', 'After a review passes, before CI. Once per run: a later round finds the
earlier shape.md and declares no findings (see simplify.md).', NULL, '$review.output.ready == true', ARRAY['review']::text[], NULL, 'archon-simplify', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'archon-deliver-block', 'deliver/archon-deliver-block.yaml');
INSERT INTO mc.arch_steps (archon_sha, factory_sha, workflow, path, parent_path, position, step_id, kind, description, model, when_condition, depends_on, trigger_rule, include, child_workflow, round_cap, command, command_file, script, script_file, runtime, bash, prompt, defined_in, file) VALUES ('57c8574020000000000000000000000000000000', '6311108f789119a8a1a6a7c77ece21ca3a75c3e8', 'archon-ship-block', 'deliver/rounds/simplify/simplify', 'deliver/rounds/simplify', 39, 'simplify', 'command', NULL, '@review-simplify @reviewer medium', NULL, '{}'::text[], NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'simplify', 'simplify/commands/simplify.md', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'archon-simplify', 'simplify/archon-simplify.yaml');
