judged the threads the previous round read; this agent checks each
disposition at the head and writes the reply each settled thread gets.', 'medium', '$LOOP_PREV.threads.output.open > 0', ARRAY['pr', 'review', 'rereview']::text[], 'none_failed_min_one_success', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'settle-threads', 'deliver/commands/settle-threads.md', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'archon-deliver-block', 'deliver/archon-deliver-block.yaml');
INSERT INTO mc.arch_steps (archon_sha, factory_sha, workflow, path, parent_path, position, step_id, kind, description, model, when_condition, depends_on, trigger_rule, include, child_workflow, round_cap, command, command_file, script, script_file, runtime, bash, prompt, defined_in, file) VALUES ('57c8574020000000000000000000000000000000', '6311108f789119a8a1a6a7c77ece21ca3a75c3e8', 'archon-deliver-block', 'rounds/ci', 'rounds', 46, 'ci', 'command', 'CI is the project''s full validation: implementers run only focused checks.
Fresh: CI reads the PR, not simplify''s or reshape''s conversation.', 'medium', '$review.output.ready == true && $simplify.output.findings == false || $review.output.ready == true && $simplify.output.findings == true && $rereview.output.ready == true', ARRAY['review', 'simplify', 'rereview', 'settle-threads']::text[], 'none_failed_min_one_success', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'ci', 'deliver/commands/ci.md', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'archon-deliver-block', 'deliver/archon-deliver-block.yaml');
INSERT INTO mc.arch_steps (archon_sha, factory_sha, workflow, path, parent_path, position, step_id, kind, description, model, when_condition, depends_on, trigger_rule, include, child_workflow, round_cap, command, command_file, script, script_file, runtime, bash, prompt, defined_in, file) VALUES ('57c8574020000000000000000000000000000000', '6311108f789119a8a1a6a7c77ece21ca3a75c3e8', 'archon-deliver-block', 'rounds/threads', 'rounds', 47, 'threads', 'script', 'Posts and resolves settle-threads'' answers, then reads what is still open,
after CI so threads posted during the round count.', NULL, NULL, ARRAY['pr', 'review', 'rereview', 'ci', 'settle-threads']::text[], 'none_failed_min_one_success', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'threads', 'deliver/scripts/threads.ts', 'bun', NULL, NULL, 'archon-deliver-block', 'deliver/archon-deliver-block.yaml');
INSERT INTO mc.arch_steps (archon_sha, factory_sha, workflow, path, parent_path, position, step_id, kind, description, model, when_condition, depends_on, trigger_rule, include, child_workflow, round_cap, command, command_file, script, script_file, runtime, bash, prompt, defined_in, file) VALUES ('57c8574020000000000000000000000000000000', '6311108f789119a8a1a6a7c77ece21ca3a75c3e8', 'archon-deliver-block', 'rounds/round', 'rounds', 48, 'round', 'script', '`until_bash` and the loop''s output cannot read a skipped node, so this joins
the round''s verdicts into the value the loop decides on.', NULL, NULL, ARRAY['implement', 'pr', 'review', 'rereview', 'ci', 'threads']::text[], 'all_done', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'round', 'deliver/scripts/round.ts', 'bun', NULL, NULL, 'archon-deliver-block', 'deliver/archon-deliver-block.yaml');
INSERT INTO mc.arch_steps (archon_sha, factory_sha, workflow, path, parent_path, position, step_id, kind, description, model, when_condition, depends_on, trigger_rule, include, child_workflow, round_cap, command, command_file, script, script_file, runtime, bash, prompt, defined_in, file) VALUES ('57c8574020000000000000000000000000000000', '6311108f789119a8a1a6a7c77ece21ca3a75c3e8', 'archon-deliver-block', 'update-pr-body', NULL, 49, 'update-pr-body', 'command', 'Corrections and the base merge can falsify claims the description made when the
draft opened, and an implementer can pass red the description must disclose. One
agent reads the live description and the final diff, and edits only what is no
longer true. It also links the issue: closing only when the latest review left
nothing open and no dated ruling on the issue keeps it open. It runs once the
rounds have ended, never per round;
content a round prepared for the description is that round''s pr step''s write.', 'medium', '$rounds.output.pr_url != ''''', ARRAY['rounds']::text[], NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'update-pr-body', 'deliver/commands/update-pr-body.md', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'archon-deliver-block', 'deliver/archon-deliver-block.yaml');
INSERT INTO mc.arch_steps (archon_sha, factory_sha, workflow, path, parent_path, position, step_id, kind, description, model, when_condition, depends_on, trigger_rule, include, child_workflow, round_cap, command, command_file, script, script_file, runtime, bash, prompt, defined_in, file) VALUES ('57c8574020000000000000000000000000000000', '6311108f789119a8a1a6a7c77ece21ca3a75c3e8', 'archon-deliver-block', 'outcome', NULL, 50, 'outcome', 'script', 'Composes the success-path report (scripts/outcome.ts): ready with the pull
request''s URL, or not ready with why. `report` relays it.', NULL, NULL, ARRAY['rounds', 'update-pr-body']::text[], 'none_failed_min_one_success', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'outcome', 'deliver/scripts/outcome.ts', 'bun', NULL, NULL, 'archon-deliver-block', 'deliver/archon-deliver-block.yaml');
INSERT INTO mc.arch_steps (archon_sha, factory_sha, workflow, path, parent_path, position, step_id, kind, description, model, when_condition, depends_on, trigger_rule, include, child_workflow, round_cap, command, command_file, script, script_file, runtime, bash, prompt, defined_in, file) VALUES ('57c8574020000000000000000000000000000000', '6311108f789119a8a1a6a7c77ece21ca3a75c3e8', 'archon-deliver-block', 'report', NULL, 51, 'report', 'script', 'The workflow''s terminal report on every ending. A node failure skips `outcome`
(never fails it), so `all_done` still runs this node and the binding reads null.
`always_run` because it reads discoveries its dependency edge does not carry.', NULL, NULL, ARRAY['outcome']::text[], 'all_done', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'report', 'deliver/scripts/report.ts', 'bun', NULL, NULL, 'archon-deliver-block', 'deliver/archon-deliver-block.yaml');
INSERT INTO mc.arch_steps (archon_sha, factory_sha, workflow, path, parent_path, position, step_id, kind, description, model, when_condition, depends_on, trigger_rule, include, child_workflow, round_cap, command, command_file, script, script_file, runtime, bash, prompt, defined_in, file) VALUES ('57c8574020000000000000000000000000000000', '6311108f789119a8a1a6a7c77ece21ca3a75c3e8', 'archon-implement', 'implement', NULL, 0, 'implement', 'loop', 'Run success ≠ green. The loop completes on `done`, which deliberately includes
a definitive blocked decline (green: false) — so a completed run''s status never
certifies the work. Consumers read $implement.output.green; compositions gate on
it deterministically before spending or shipping (deliver''s pr step does), and the
workflow''s outcome_field records it as the run''s authored outcome.
Each turn is a fresh session: work that continues past a seam is carried by its
commits and implementation.md, never by a conversation that grows with the work.', '@implementer large', NULL, '{}'::text[], NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'implement', 'implement/commands/implement.md', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'archon-implement', 'implement/archon-implement.yaml');
INSERT INTO mc.arch_steps (archon_sha, factory_sha, workflow, path, parent_path, position, step_id, kind, description, model, when_condition, depends_on, trigger_rule, include, child_workflow, round_cap, command, command_file, script, script_file, runtime, bash, prompt, defined_in, file) VALUES ('57c8574020000000000000000000000000000000', '6311108f789119a8a1a6a7c77ece21ca3a75c3e8', 'archon-pr', 'forge', NULL, 0, 'forge', 'script', 'Refuses the run before the agent spends when the selected forge source cannot
act: no plugin for the host, no usable credential, or an unauthenticated gh.', NULL, NULL, '{}'::text[], NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'forge-check', 'pr/scripts/forge-check.ts', 'bun', NULL, NULL, 'archon-pr', 'pr/archon-pr.yaml');
INSERT INTO mc.arch_steps (archon_sha, factory_sha, workflow, path, parent_path, position, step_id, kind, description, model, when_condition, depends_on, trigger_rule, include, child_workflow, round_cap, command, command_file, script, script_file, runtime, bash, prompt, defined_in, file) VALUES ('57c8574020000000000000000000000000000000', '6311108f789119a8a1a6a7c77ece21ca3a75c3e8', 'archon-pr', 'prepare', NULL, 1, 'prepare', 'command', 'The agent judges: which repository the work is proposed to, the base, whether
the run continues an existing pull request, and what the title and body say.
It performs no push and no forge write.', 'medium', NULL, ARRAY['forge']::text[], NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'pr', 'pr/commands/pr.md', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'archon-pr', 'pr/archon-pr.yaml');
INSERT INTO mc.arch_steps (archon_sha, factory_sha, workflow, path, parent_path, position, step_id, kind, description, model, when_condition, depends_on, trigger_rule, include, child_workflow, round_cap, command, command_file, script, script_file, runtime, bash, prompt, defined_in, file) VALUES ('57c8574020000000000000000000000000000000', '6311108f789119a8a1a6a7c77ece21ca3a75c3e8', 'archon-pr', 'publish', NULL, 2, 'publish', 'script', 'The durable ownership record for every later public action in delivery and
inbound forge event. It pushes the branch, then opens the pull request, or
reuses the one this work already has; consumers use this qualified identity,
never gh''s ambient branch lookup.', NULL, NULL, ARRAY['prepare']::text[], NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'publish-pr', 'pr/scripts/publish-pr.ts', 'bun', NULL, NULL, 'archon-pr', 'pr/archon-pr.yaml');
INSERT INTO mc.arch_steps (archon_sha, factory_sha, workflow, path, parent_path, position, step_id, kind, description, model, when_condition, depends_on, trigger_rule, include, child_workflow, round_cap, command, command_file, script, script_file, runtime, bash, prompt, defined_in, file) VALUES ('57c8574020000000000000000000000000000000', '6311108f789119a8a1a6a7c77ece21ca3a75c3e8', 'archon-review-block', 'policy', NULL, 0, 'policy', 'script', 'The directory of the pack''s default policy documents in this run''s captured
source, the same in a source checkout and a binary install. Synthesis names the
policy file it needs and reads the default, then the project''s own on top.', NULL, NULL, '{}'::text[], NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'policy', 'review/scripts/policy.ts', 'bun', NULL, NULL, 'archon-review-block', 'review/archon-review-block.yaml');
INSERT INTO mc.arch_steps (archon_sha, factory_sha, workflow, path, parent_path, position, step_id, kind, description, model, when_condition, depends_on, trigger_rule, include, child_workflow, round_cap, command, command_file, script, script_file, runtime, bash, prompt, defined_in, file) VALUES ('57c8574020000000000000000000000000000000', '6311108f789119a8a1a6a7c77ece21ca3a75c3e8', 'archon-review-block', 'mode', NULL, 1, 'mode', 'script', 'After scope accepts the checkout, fixes what this round reviews: whether it
continues a previous round, the commit under review (the checkout''s HEAD as
the engine observed it), and, on a continuation, the previous round''s
reviewed commit, which the head must descend from. A caller''s pull-request
record names the PR, never the commit: its head revision goes stale with
every push after the PR opens. publish refuses a report about any other
commit. The node also turns the input into the routable fact the lenses gate
on: an include''s inputs are substituted as text at load time and cannot be
compared in a `when:`. For the same reason it carries the part assignment, so
synthesis reads a value certified against its schema, not raw text.', NULL, '$scope.output.head_matches == true', ARRAY['scope']::text[], NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'review-round', 'review/scripts/review-round.ts', 'bun', NULL, NULL, 'archon-review-block', 'review/archon-review-block.yaml');
INSERT INTO mc.arch_steps (archon_sha, factory_sha, workflow, path, parent_path, position, step_id, kind, description, model, when_condition, depends_on, trigger_rule, include, child_workflow, round_cap, command, command_file, script, script_file, runtime, bash, prompt, defined_in, file) VALUES ('57c8574020000000000000000000000000000000', '6311108f789119a8a1a6a7c77ece21ca3a75c3e8', 'archon-review-block', 'review-dir', NULL, 2, 'review-dir', 'bash', 'Every review node writes under review/, and a fresh run''s artifacts directory
has none. Agents told to create it have skipped that step, so the declared
scope.md pointer failed and took the whole delivery run down with it.', NULL, NULL, '{}'::text[], NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'mkdir -p "$ARTIFACTS_DIR/review"', NULL, 'archon-review-block', 'review/archon-review-block.yaml');
INSERT INTO mc.arch_steps (archon_sha, factory_sha, workflow, path, parent_path, position, step_id, kind, description, model, when_condition, depends_on, trigger_rule, include, child_workflow, round_cap, command, command_file, script, script_file, runtime, bash, prompt, defined_in, file) VALUES ('57c8574020000000000000000000000000000000', '6311108f789119a8a1a6a7c77ece21ca3a75c3e8', 'archon-review-block', 'scope', NULL, 3, 'scope', 'command', NULL, '@reviewer medium', NULL, ARRAY['review-dir']::text[], NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'review-scope', 'review/commands/review-scope.md', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'archon-review-block', 'review/archon-review-block.yaml');
INSERT INTO mc.arch_steps (archon_sha, factory_sha, workflow, path, parent_path, position, step_id, kind, description, model, when_condition, depends_on, trigger_rule, include, child_workflow, round_cap, command, command_file, script, script_file, runtime, bash, prompt, defined_in, file) VALUES ('57c8574020000000000000000000000000000000', '6311108f789119a8a1a6a7c77ece21ca3a75c3e8', 'archon-review-block', 'route', NULL, 4, 'route', 'command', 'After scope checks the head, a small model reads the diff
summary and the work order and answers, with seams on by default. Every round
but a light one routes; on a continuation route adds to the code lens every lens
whose finding the previous report leaves open or whose area the delta touches.', 'small', '$scope.output.head_matches == true && $mode.output.light == false', ARRAY['mode', 'scope']::text[], NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'route-review', 'review/commands/route-review.md', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'archon-review-block', 'review/archon-review-block.yaml');
INSERT INTO mc.arch_steps (archon_sha, factory_sha, workflow, path, parent_path, position, step_id, kind, description, model, when_condition, depends_on, trigger_rule, include, child_workflow, round_cap, command, command_file, script, script_file, runtime, bash, prompt, defined_in, file) VALUES ('57c8574020000000000000000000000000000000', '6311108f789119a8a1a6a7c77ece21ca3a75c3e8', 'archon-review-block', 'seams', NULL, 5, 'seams', 'command', '── Lenses ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Every reviewer is read-only by the engine''s check, not only by its prompt:
lenses run in parallel in one checkout, so a reviewer that edits it can
mislead the others. `&&` binds tighter than `||` and short-circuits, so a
light round, which skips the route node, never reads it.', '@review-seams @reviewer medium', '$scope.output.head_matches == true && $mode.output.light == false && $route.output.seams == true || $scope.output.head_matches == true && $mode.output.seams == true', ARRAY['scope', 'route']::text[], 'none_failed_min_one_success', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'review-seams', 'review/commands/review-seams.md', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'archon-review-block', 'review/archon-review-block.yaml');
INSERT INTO mc.arch_steps (archon_sha, factory_sha, workflow, path, parent_path, position, step_id, kind, description, model, when_condition, depends_on, trigger_rule, include, child_workflow, round_cap, command, command_file, script, script_file, runtime, bash, prompt, defined_in, file) VALUES ('57c8574020000000000000000000000000000000', '6311108f789119a8a1a6a7c77ece21ca3a75c3e8', 'archon-review-block', 'code', NULL, 6, 'code', 'command', NULL, '@review-code @reviewer large', '$scope.output.head_matches == true && $mode.output.light == false && $route.output.code == true || $scope.output.head_matches == true && $mode.output.code == true', ARRAY['scope', 'route']::text[], 'none_failed_min_one_success', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'review-code', 'review/commands/review-code.md', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'archon-review-block', 'review/archon-review-block.yaml');
INSERT INTO mc.arch_steps (archon_sha, factory_sha, workflow, path, parent_path, position, step_id, kind, description, model, when_condition, depends_on, trigger_rule, include, child_workflow, round_cap, command, command_file, script, script_file, runtime, bash, prompt, defined_in, file) VALUES ('57c8574020000000000000000000000000000000', '6311108f789119a8a1a6a7c77ece21ca3a75c3e8', 'archon-review-block', 'tests', NULL, 7, 'tests', 'command', NULL, '@review-tests @reviewer medium', '$scope.output.head_matches == true && $mode.output.light == false && $route.output.tests == true || $scope.output.head_matches == true && $mode.output.tests == true', ARRAY['scope', 'route']::text[], 'none_failed_min_one_success', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'review-tests', 'review/commands/review-tests.md', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'archon-review-block', 'review/archon-review-block.yaml');
INSERT INTO mc.arch_steps (archon_sha, factory_sha, workflow, path, parent_path, position, step_id, kind, description, model, when_condition, depends_on, trigger_rule, include, child_workflow, round_cap, command, command_file, script, script_file, runtime, bash, prompt, defined_in, file) VALUES ('57c8574020000000000000000000000000000000', '6311108f789119a8a1a6a7c77ece21ca3a75c3e8', 'archon-review-block', 'errors', NULL, 8, 'errors', 'command', NULL, '@review-errors @reviewer medium', '$scope.output.head_matches == true && $mode.output.light == false && $route.output.errors == true || $scope.output.head_matches == true && $mode.output.errors == true', ARRAY['scope', 'route']::text[], 'none_failed_min_one_success', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'review-errors', 'review/commands/review-errors.md', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'archon-review-block', 'review/archon-review-block.yaml');
INSERT INTO mc.arch_steps (archon_sha, factory_sha, workflow, path, parent_path, position, step_id, kind, description, model, when_condition, depends_on, trigger_rule, include, child_workflow, round_cap, command, command_file, script, script_file, runtime, bash, prompt, defined_in, file) VALUES ('57c8574020000000000000000000000000000000', '6311108f789119a8a1a6a7c77ece21ca3a75c3e8', 'archon-review-block', 'docs', NULL, 9, 'docs', 'command', NULL, '@review-docs @reviewer medium', '$scope.output.head_matches == true && $mode.output.light == false && $route.output.docs == true || $scope.output.head_matches == true && $mode.output.docs == true', ARRAY['scope', 'route']::text[], 'none_failed_min_one_success', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'review-docs', 'review/commands/review-docs.md', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'archon-review-block', 'review/archon-review-block.yaml');
INSERT INTO mc.arch_steps (archon_sha, factory_sha, workflow, path, parent_path, position, step_id, kind, description, model, when_condition, depends_on, trigger_rule, include, child_workflow, round_cap, command, command_file, script, script_file, runtime, bash, prompt, defined_in, file) VALUES ('57c8574020000000000000000000000000000000', '6311108f789119a8a1a6a7c77ece21ca3a75c3e8', 'archon-review-block', 'review-complete', NULL, 10, 'review-complete', 'bash', 'all_done lets this barrier settle after unselected lenses, or a lens whose
retries were exhausted. The deciding
agent can then tolerate specialist failures without also tolerating a failed
mode/scope preflight: synthesize separately requires both to have succeeded.', NULL, '$scope.output.head_matches == true', ARRAY['scope', 'route', 'seams', 'code', 'tests', 'errors', 'docs']::text[], 'all_done', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'true', NULL, 'archon-review-block', 'review/archon-review-block.yaml');
INSERT INTO mc.arch_steps (archon_sha, factory_sha, workflow, path, parent_path, position, step_id, kind, description, model, when_condition, depends_on, trigger_rule, include, child_workflow, round_cap, command, command_file, script, script_file, runtime, bash, prompt, defined_in, file) VALUES ('57c8574020000000000000000000000000000000', '6311108f789119a8a1a6a7c77ece21ca3a75c3e8', 'archon-review-block', 'synthesize', NULL, 11, 'synthesize', 'command', 'A failed specialist (a provider stream dying mid-review, say) must not kill
the review: synthesize detects the missing completion for a selected lens and
forces ready:false naming the gap, so degradation is disclosed, never silent,
and the next round is the retry. `ready` is a real boolean — the load-bearing field a composing
loop terminates on. Every round receives this round''s lens files; a
continuation also receives the complete prior report and correction delta.

The deciding agent and the lenses start fresh and carry earlier rounds through
the prior report, not a resumed session: a loop body cannot resume a session
from its own earlier iteration, and session resume is not portable across the
bundle''s supported providers (Claude Code, Codex, and Pi).

Adversarial per-finding verification happens inside this node''s prompt. A
separate verify stage between the lenses and this node is now expressible and
would not change either side''s contract — the findings files are the declared
boundary — but nothing has measured it as better than the in-prompt pass, so
it stays here until something does.', '@reviewer medium', '$scope.output.head_matches == true', ARRAY['policy', 'mode', 'scope', 'review-complete']::text[], NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'review-synthesize', 'review/commands/review-synthesize.md', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'archon-review-block', 'review/archon-review-block.yaml');
INSERT INTO mc.arch_steps (archon_sha, factory_sha, workflow, path, parent_path, position, step_id, kind, description, model, when_condition, depends_on, trigger_rule, include, child_workflow, round_cap, command, command_file, script, script_file, runtime, bash, prompt, defined_in, file) VALUES ('57c8574020000000000000000000000000000000', '6311108f789119a8a1a6a7c77ece21ca3a75c3e8', 'archon-review-block', 'publish', NULL, 12, 'publish', 'script', 'The reviewer judges and writes the report; this node owns the one public
write, so every round edits the same marked comment instead of appending
another, through whichever forge source the run selected (on `gh`, a landed
write that returned a retryable response (5xx, or a rate limit) or no response can leave a second one, and the next
upsert refuses). The verdict passes
through unchanged: publication is not what makes a review true.', NULL, '$scope.output.head_matches == true', ARRAY['synthesize']::text[], NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'publish-review', 'review/scripts/publish-review.ts', 'bun', NULL, NULL, 'archon-review-block', 'review/archon-review-block.yaml');
INSERT INTO mc.arch_steps (archon_sha, factory_sha, workflow, path, parent_path, position, step_id, kind, description, model, when_condition, depends_on, trigger_rule, include, child_workflow, round_cap, command, command_file, script, script_file, runtime, bash, prompt, defined_in, file) VALUES ('57c8574020000000000000000000000000000000', '6311108f789119a8a1a6a7c77ece21ca3a75c3e8', 'archon-review-block', 'result', NULL, 13, 'result', 'script', 'Standalone runs show the first completed sink, so the verdict precedes cleanup.', NULL, NULL, ARRAY['scope', 'publish']::text[], 'none_failed_min_one_success', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'const verdict = JSON.parse(process.env.INPUTS_VERDICT);
const report = JSON.parse(process.env.INPUTS_SCOPE_REPORT);
console.log(JSON.stringify(JSON.parse(process.env.INPUTS_HEAD_MATCHES) ? verdict : {
  ready: false, action: "ask",
  findings_summary: require("node:fs").readFileSync(require("node:path").join(process.env.ARTIFACTS_DIR, report.path), "utf8"),
  report, discoveries: [], contract_left: ["PR head mismatch prevented contract review."]
}));
', NULL, 'bun', NULL, NULL, 'archon-review-block', 'review/archon-review-block.yaml');
INSERT INTO mc.arch_steps (archon_sha, factory_sha, workflow, path, parent_path, position, step_id, kind, description, model, when_condition, depends_on, trigger_rule, include, child_workflow, round_cap, command, command_file, script, script_file, runtime, bash, prompt, defined_in, file) VALUES ('57c8574020000000000000000000000000000000', '6311108f789119a8a1a6a7c77ece21ca3a75c3e8', 'archon-review-block', 'prune-scratch', NULL, 14, 'prune-scratch', 'script', 'Reviewers'' scratch worktrees are removed by the workflow once every lens and
the deciding agent have settled, whether they succeeded or failed.', NULL, NULL, ARRAY['synthesize']::text[], 'all_done', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'prune-scratch', 'review/scripts/prune-scratch.ts', 'bun', NULL, NULL, 'archon-review-block', 'review/archon-review-block.yaml');
INSERT INTO mc.arch_steps (archon_sha, factory_sha, workflow, path, parent_path, position, step_id, kind, description, model, when_condition, depends_on, trigger_rule, include, child_workflow, round_cap, command, command_file, script, script_file, runtime, bash, prompt, defined_in, file) VALUES ('57c8574020000000000000000000000000000000', '6311108f789119a8a1a6a7c77ece21ca3a75c3e8', 'archon-simplify', 'simplify', NULL, 0, 'simplify', 'command', NULL, '@review-simplify @reviewer medium', NULL, '{}'::text[], NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'simplify', 'simplify/commands/simplify.md', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'archon-simplify', 'simplify/archon-simplify.yaml');
